From cb9c358a129f1500e2a7001a5b074e76f1d8c97b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 00:19:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] mm: make mapping_mapped aware of i_mmap shards

Future sharded i_mmap users will no longer keep the central interval
tree as the only source of mapped-state information.  Prepare the
lightweight mapping_mapped() query to handle that state before
write-side conversion is enabled.

If sharded state has been published, use the aggregate VMA counter
maintained by the shard owner.  Otherwise keep the existing central
tree check unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
---
 include/linux/fs.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/fs.h b/include/linux/fs.h
index 53b47a8f2306..51a9e07e4e9f 100644
--- a/include/linux/fs.h
+++ b/include/linux/fs.h
@@ -605,6 +605,11 @@ static inline void i_mmap_assert_write_locked(struct address_space *mapping)
  */
 static inline int mapping_mapped(struct address_space *mapping)
 {
+	struct i_mmap_shards *shards = READ_ONCE(mapping->i_mmap_shards);
+
+	if (shards)
+		return atomic_read(&shards->nr_vmas) > 0;
+
 	return	!RB_EMPTY_ROOT(&mapping->i_mmap.rb_root);
 }
 
